{
  "id": "unsampled-entrypoint-binary",
  "title": "A release points a new bin command at a file the review cannot read",
  "category": "obfuscated-dropper",
  "intent": "The release adds a bin whose target has a non-script extension and binary-looking content. npm links it onto the consumer's PATH and Node runs it as JavaScript whatever its extension, but the parser keeps no text sample for a binary body, so no content rule can read it. file.unsampled-entrypoint reports the unreadable entrypoint; diff.bin-added reports the new command. The body is represented only by its FileRecord metadata.",
